{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLQ5XwoePNHTeqcp6bec","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I could not find the community decision or the ticket that fixes the reload bug. Patient-chart pull requests are not ingested in Falkon, and the discussion search returned nothing for this topic. What the code does show:\n\n- **The conditions list reads a different data source.** `useConditions` fetches FHIR `Condition` resources filtered to the `problem-list-item` category (`packages/esm-patient-conditions-app/src/conditions/conditions.resource.ts:129-152`). A visit-note diagnosis is saved as an encounter diagnosis with `condition: null` (`packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.component.tsx:456-466`), so it does not create a problem-list Condition.\n- **The save path does not refresh the conditions list.** After a note is saved, the form calls `invalidateVisitAndEncounterData` and `mutateVisitNotes` (`visit-notes-form.component.tsx:517-519`). That helper only invalidates visit history and patient encounters (`packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.ts:117-120`), not the conditions SWR key. So a reload is the only refresh path for the conditions widget.\n- **Related visit-level fixes.** O3-5822 (commit `1a2af778`) added `dedupeDiagnoses` so repeated diagnoses across a visit's encounters collapse to one entry, with the primary rank winning. It is wired into the visit diagnoses cell and the visit summary. O3-5823 (commit `d0f4b1bf`) captured diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note, and its esm-core counterpart (PR 1881) added certainty display to the shared diagnosis tags. Its patch is too large to read in full here.\n\nWhether the community wanted the conditions list to show visit-note diagnoses, and which ticket fixed the reload, would need the patient-chart PR discussion (e.g. #3621 or #3496), which Falkon has not imported. The entries below are the closest evidence I found, not a confirmed answer to the reload question.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-conditions-app/src/conditions/conditions.resource.ts\", \"startLine\": 129, \"endLine\": 152},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 444, \"endLine\": 468},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 514, \"endLine\": 524},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.ts\", \"startLine\": 102, \"endLine\": 120},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/dedupe-diagnoses.ts\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 76},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/dedupe-diagnoses.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 63},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visit-history-table/visit-diagnoses-cell.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 18},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visits-widget/past-visits-components/visit-summary.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 15, \"endLine\": 18},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 651, \"endLine\": 651},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"commit\": \"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"commit\": \"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"pr\": 3496},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"pr\": 3621},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-core\", \"pr\": 1881},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-5822\"},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-5823\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequen